## Input

You can receive a request with a token. The server is expected to receive a request with a token.

```json
{
  "token": ""
}
```

The token is a JSON Web Token (JWT). It has the following format.

```json
{
  "aud": "application",
  "exp": <timestamp>,
  "iat": <timestamp>,
  "iss": "server",
  "jti": "bfef9bd8-4ce3-4fb6-a206-371e491ef8c1",
  "sub": "user",
  "user_id": "1e2af231-a06c-40c9-87ec-f96772f1e748",
  "alg": "HS256",
  "scope": "user"
}
```

## Output

If the token was verified to be `HS256`, the server will respond with the following response body.

```json
{
  "status": "ok"
}
```

If the token was not verified, the server will respond with the following response body.

```json
{
  "status": "fail",
  "message": "Invalid token"
}
```

