# How to print "Hello World" in an infinite loop?

## Solution 1

Use `system("pause")` or `system("read -p 'Press a key to continue...'"` for Windows or `read -p 'Press a key to continue...'` for Unix.

## Solution 2

Use `fflush(stdout);` to print continuously.

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    while (1) {
        printf("Hello World\n");
        fflush(stdout);
    }
    return 0;
}
```

## Solution 3

Use `getch()` or `getche()` for using `pause` in Windows.

```c
#include <conio.h>

int main() {
    while (1) {
        printf("Hello World\n");
        getch();
    }
    return 0;
}
```
