# How to count number of digits in double or float number?

## Solution using `log10` function

```c
#include <math.h>

int countDigits(double num) {
    return (int) (log10(fabs(num))+1);
}

int main() {
    printf("%d", countDigits(123456789.0));
    return 0;
}
```

## Solution using `ceil` and `floor` functions

```c
#include <math.h>

int countDigits(double num) {
    return (int) (num >= 0? ceil(log10(num)) : floor(log10(-num)));
}

int main() {
    printf("%d", countDigits(123456789.0));
    return 0;
}
```
