Process p = Runtime.getRuntime().exec(cmd);

This will actually launch a command prompt, and it will run the cmd. But since we are executing via Runtime, the shell will be set to whatever the user's default shell is, which is usually not what we want. What we want is to run the command line from the Java process. To do so, we use Runtime.getRuntime().exec(new String[]{"cmd.exe", "/c", cmd}) instead, which will run the command line within the Java process.
